  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh RRNRP (Objective 1) - Contribution to IOM Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh under Capital Development(CDEL) component.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide multisectoral humanitarian support Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh with Capital Development through IOM in Bangladesh which is an ODA eligible country. Bangladesh is one of the least developed countries under the Current DAC list of ODA recipients.
With over one million Rohingya, Cox&apos;s Bazar is the world&apos;s most significant refugee settlement, where refugees reside in 33 extremely congested camps. The activities under this component would include building or renovating Shelters, Site Management and Site Development (including Slope Stabilization, Training Center Renovation), reconstructing Water Sanitation and Hygiene systems and setting up and renovating Women Friendly spaces for protection and hospitals in the Cox&apos;s Bazar camps.</narrative>
  </description>
